    "grp_igbp": {
      "igbp": "WET",
      "igbp_comment": "The plant community  is a mix of C3 and C4 species. The vegetation exhibits a zonation based on hydrologic tolerance of species. The edge zone of the wetland is diverse and composed of Panicum hemi_x0002_tomon (25–50%), other grasses (10–20%; Panicum longifolium Andropogon glomeratus var. glaucopsis), Juncus effusus (~30%), sedges (5–10%; Cyperus sp., Rhynchospora sp., and Eleocharis sp.), and Woodwardia\nvirginica (5–10%). Forbs are also present but have patchy distribution and low cover (Centella asiatica, Alternanthera philoxeroides, Diodia virginiana, and Ludwigia repens). In the deeper hydrologic zone of the wetland, Panicum hemitomon dominates with approximately 70–90% cover. Other species in this zone\ninclude Sagittaria lancifolia, Pontederia cordata, and Cephalanthus occidentalis. In the deepest zone of this wetland, there is a patch of Salix caroliniana."
    },
